🧮 Day 31: Calculator Using Functions — Phase 3 Begins!

📌 Project Overview

Welcome to Phase 3: Functions, File Handling, and Exceptions! 🎉

In Day 31, I rewrote the Day 2 calculator using Python functions. Instead of writing all calculation logic inside one long block, each mathematical operation has its own reusable function.

The calculator supports addition, subtraction, multiplication, division, exponentiation, and modulus. It also handles division by zero and prevents invalid menu choices from crashing the program.

This project introduces an important programming habit: write code once and reuse it whenever needed.


